[0m## Guffin Contribution Checklist: Sampling/Cache Logic Changes

This checklist guides changes to Guffin's sampling or cache logic, ensuring correctness and performance.

**I. Design & Planning (Before Coding)**

*   [ ] **Problem Definition:** Clearly define the measured whole-path problem this change addresses.
*   [ ] **Upper Bound:** Estimate the plausible maximum end-to-end performance improvement.
*   [ ] **Ownership & Invariants:** Identify impacted ownership, layout, lifetime, and synchronization invariants.
*   [ ] **Simplicity:** Prioritize removing work over complex optimizations.
*   [ ] **Rationale:** Document *why* this design was chosen over alternatives.

**II. Automated Correctness Checks (Mandatory)**

*   [ ] **Type Validation:** Ensure changes preserve data types and validity.
*   [ ] **Unit Tests:** Add deterministic tests for changed behavior and regressions.
*   [ ] **Lossless Sampling Test:** Verify preservation of the configured sampling distribution (`tests/engine/lossless_sampling_tests.cpp`).
*   [ ] **Metal Numerical Tests:** Confirm correctness of packed projections & fused sums (`tests/tensor/gemma3_metal_tests.cpp`).
*   [ ] **Target Runtime Tests:** Validate target equations, local cache wrap, and callback receipts (`tests/engine/gemma3_target_runtime_tests.cpp`).
*   [ ] **Tensor Admission Tests:** Ensure descriptors are validated and views check backing storage (`tests/tensor/tensor_tests.cpp`).

**III. Actual Chat Performance Measurement (Post-Correctness)**

*   [ ] **Representative Inputs:** Test with realistic prompts & conversations.
*   [ ] **Release Build:** Benchmark using an optimized build.
*   [ ] **Variance & Thermals:** Control for system variability (thermals, background load).
*   [ ] **Whole-Path Improvement:** Verify a measurable, positive impact on chat performance.



**Important Notes:**

*   Refer to `ENGINE_PRINCIPLES.md` for coding standards.
*   Document all assumptions and tradeoffs clearly.
